# 05-aiter-kimik3-fused-tuned-gemm.diff
#
# aiter tuned-GEMM table entries for the two bf16 shapes sglang synthesises for
# Kimi-K3 by merging weights, which no shipped CSV covers:
#   N=6016 K=7168   the fused MoE front  [shared gate_up | router gate | latent down]
#   N=144  K=7168   the merged KDA b/f/a GEMV  [f_a | b], 132 rows padded to 144
# M = 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024 for each.
#
# Origin:  mine, but not hand-written -- produced by aiter's own multi-backend
#          tuner, unmodified:
#            cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && python3 csrc/gemm_a16w16/gemm_a16w16_tune.py \
#              -i  <workspace>/analysis/gemm_tune/untuned_k3_fused.csv \
#              -o  <workspace>/analysis/gemm_tune/tuned_k3_fused.csv \
#              --libtype all --with-hipblaslt --all
#          ~25 min on 8 idle MI355X; it searches asm/opus/flydsl/triton/skinny/
#          torch plus ~2000 hipBLASLt solutions per shape. Input and output are
#          both kept in analysis/gemm_tune/ so the file can be regenerated.
# Base:    aiter git 68e42f5f461556596ae294200f1a3f13378c8582 (checkout at
#          /sgl-workspace/aiter). The file is new, so the pristine state is
#          "absent".
# Apply:   cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && git apply <this file> \
#            && rm -f /tmp/aiter_configs/bf16_tuned_gemm.csv
#          The rm matters: aiter merges configs/bf16_tuned_gemm.csv with every
#          model_configs/*bf16_tuned_gemm*.csv into that cached file at import,
#          and a stale cache silently ignores the new rows.
# Pairs with: 04-fused-front-gemm-via-aiter.diff, which is what makes sglang
#          consult the table for these shapes. On its own this file changes
#          nothing -- no call site reaches these shapes through aiter without 04.
#
# Note on the N=144 rows: they are tuned and correct, but no call site uses them
# today. That GEMV goes through sglang.kernels.ops.kimi_k3.kimi_k3_tiny_gemm,
# whose m<=16 dispatch limit sends bs 63 to F.linear; routing its fallback to
# aiter measures 1.051x, which is 0.17% of decode and below the noise floor, so
# the code change was not made. Rows kept so the shape is covered if it is.
#
# End-to-end: arm D (01+02+03+04+05) 949.964 tok/s, mean of 7 settled runs over
#          2 server restarts (sd 2.606), against arm C (01+02) 936.952, mean of
#          10 runs over 3 restarts (sd 1.318): +1.389%, which is 1.95x this
#          machine's 0.713% across-restart noise floor. +18.19% over the local
#          baseline of 803.786. gsm8k 5-shot strict-match 0.9788 +/- 0.0040
#          (gate 0.9765 +/- 0.0042), eval_results/candD_s7_20260820_163121.
diff --git a/aiter/configs/model_configs/kimik3fused_bf16_tuned_gemm.csv b/aiter/configs/model_configs/kimik3fused_bf16_tuned_gemm.csv
new file mode 100644
